>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `model_refute`

``` hol4
Refute.model_refute : term -> outcome
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runs Refute's finite model finder.

`Refute.model_refute tm` calls `Refute.refute` using
`!Refute.the_config` after forcing backend selection to
`SOME ["kodkod"]`.  Every other field of the current configuration is
preserved, including finite scopes, solver and encoding options, output
controls, quiet mode, and expectations.

The `kodkod` backend is configured only when the external Kodkodi
component is available.  If it is unavailable, the result is `Unknown`
with a no-configured-backend reason.  A reconstructed model's certainty is
determined by the soundness and exactness of its encoding, independently of
whether Refute constructs a HOL certificate.  Thus a Kodkodi result may be
`Genuine` with `cert = NONE`; `cert = SOME thm` additionally records a HOL
theorem certifying the counterexample.

